      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that Kconfig doesn\u0027t have direct support for enums.  I can see 2 possible approaches:\n\nCreate an \"int\" type Kconfig, and use the help text to describe the colors.  Similar to this: https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/91d4b7766ceee7fabb5caa026ba181c47286e28b/subsys/mgmt/updatehub/Kconfig#L99\n\nCreate a choice type in Kconfig.\n\nchoice CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR\n    prompt \"Charging near full LED color\"\n    default CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_AMBER\n    \nconfig CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_AMBER\n    bool \"amber\"\n    \nconfig CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_GREEN\n    bool \"green\"\nendchoice\n\nconfig PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR\n    int\n    default 1 if CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_GREEN\n    default 5 if CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_AMBER\n    \nThe platform would then add\n\nchoice CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR\n    default CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR_GREEN\n    \nconfig_chip.h would use (regardless of approach):\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_NEAR_FULL_COLOR \\\n    CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_NEAR_FULL_COLOR",
